Here's a complete example:

**XAML (ItemsPage.xaml)**

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.Views.ItemsPage">

    <RefreshView Command="{Binding RefreshCommand}"
                 IsRefreshing="{Binding IsRefreshing}">

        <CollectionView ItemsSource="{Binding Items}"
                        SelectionMode="Single"
                        SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedItem}"
                        SelectionChangedCommand="{Binding SelectionChangedCommand}">
            <CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
                <DataTemplate>
                    <VerticalStackLayout Padding="10">
                        <Label Text="{Binding Name}" FontSize="18" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding Description}" FontSize="14" TextColor="Gray" />
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </DataTemplate>
            </CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
        </CollectionView>

    </RefreshView>
</ContentPage>
```

**ViewModel (ItemsViewModel.cs)**

```csharp
public partial class ItemsViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    private readonly IApiService _api;
    private readonly INavigationService _nav;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private ObservableCollection<Item> items = new();

    [ObservableProperty]
    private bool isRefreshing;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private Item? selectedItem;

    public ItemsViewModel(IApiService api, INavigationService nav)
    {
        _api = api;
        _nav = nav;
    }

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task Refresh()
    {
        var data = await _api.GetItemsAsync();
        Items = new ObservableCollection<Item>(data);
        IsRefreshing = false; // stops the refresh spinner
    }

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task SelectionChanged()
    {
        if (SelectedItem is null) return;

        await _nav.GoToAsync("DetailPage", new Dictionary<string, object>
        {
            ["Item"] = SelectedItem
        });

        SelectedItem = null; // reset so user can re-select same item
    }
}
```

**Key binding relationships:**

| XAML Property | ViewModel Property | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `RefreshView.Command` | `RefreshCommand` | Triggers API reload on pull |
| `RefreshView.IsRefreshing` | `IsRefreshing` | Controls spinner visibility |
| `CollectionView.ItemsSource` | `Items` | The data collection |
| `CollectionView.SelectedItem` | `SelectedItem` | Two-way; tracks selection |
| `SelectionChangedCommand` | `SelectionChangedCommand` | Fires navigation logic |

**Important notes:**

- Set `IsRefreshing = false` after loading completes, or the spinner never stops.
- Reset `SelectedItem = null` after navigation so the same row can be tapped again.
- Uses `CommunityToolkit.Mvvm` source generators (`[ObservableProperty]`, `[RelayCommand]`).
- `SelectionMode="Single"` ensures only one item highlights at a time.
